@page "/faq"

<h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>

<p class="text-muted">
    This app supports two types of uploads:
    <strong>JSON uploads</strong> for developers who want to provide structured data with categories,
    and <strong>receipt uploads</strong> (images, PDFs) for end‑users who rely on OCR and machine learning
    to automatically categorize expenses. The FAQ below explains how each path works.
</p>

<div class="accordion" id="faqAccordion">
    <!-- JSON Uploads -->
    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header" id="headingJson">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#collapseJson" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseJson">
                Do JSON uploads require a category?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="collapseJson" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingJson"
             data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                Yes. JSON uploads must include a <code>category</code> field. If it’s missing, the upload fails.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Receipt Uploads -->
    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header" id="headingReceipts">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#collapseReceipts" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseReceipts">
                How are handwritten receipts handled?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="collapseReceipts" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingReceipts"
             data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                Handwritten receipts, PDFs, or images don’t require categories. The app uses OCR + ML.NET
                to predict categories automatically.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Uploading Receipts -->
    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header" id="headingOne">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#collapseOne" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseOne">
                How do I upload receipts?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="collapseOne" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingOne"
             data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                You can upload handwritten receipts, PDFs, images, or JSON files directly from the dashboard.
                OCR extracts text and ML.NET predicts categories automatically.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Sample Files -->
    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header" id="headingSamples">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#collapseSamples" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseSamples">
                Can I use sample files to test?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="collapseSamples" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingSamples"
             data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                Yes. A dedicated <a href="/samples">Samples page</a> provides example receipts, JSON files,
                and invoices you can download and upload here. These examples are optional and meant to
                demonstrate supported formats — you can also upload your own files.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>


    <!-- Complex vs Simple PDFs -->
    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header" id="headingComplex">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#collapseComplex" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseComplex">
                Why do complex business invoices parse differently than simple receipts?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="collapseComplex" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingComplex"
             data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                Simple handwritten or straightforward receipts (e.g., a list of items and amounts) parse cleanly
                with OCR and categorization. Complex business‑style invoices, such as corporate tax invoices,
                often include tables, subtotals, discounts, taxes, and metadata. OCR flattens these structures
                into text, which can cause extra words to be captured and flagged for correction.
                <br /><br />
                This tool is optimized for handwritten receipts and everyday expenses. Complex invoices are not
                the primary focus, and may require manual correction if uploaded.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Flagged Rows -->
    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header" id="headingFlagged">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#collapseFlagged" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseFlagged">
                What does it mean when an expense is flagged for correction?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="collapseFlagged" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingFlagged"
             data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                When OCR or parsing cannot confidently extract an amount or description, the entry is flagged.
                For example, rows with <code>Amount = 0</code> or uncertain text are highlighted in the dashboard.
                This ensures data integrity by prompting you to review and correct those entries before reports
                are generated. The correction loop is part of the app’s design to balance automation with
                human oversight.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Data Safety -->
    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header" id="headingTwo">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#collapseTwo" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseTwo">
                Is my data safe?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="collapseTwo" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingTwo"
             data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                Yes. Data is processed only within this application and trusted Microsoft Azure services
                (OCR, PDF generation, secure database). No data is shared with unauthorized third parties.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Categorization -->
    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header" id="headingThree">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#collapseThree" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseThree">
                Can I change the categories?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="collapseThree" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingThree"
             data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                No. Categories are automatically assigned by the app and are read‑only for non-JSON uploads.
                This ensures consistency and demonstrates the tool’s ability to categorize handwritten receipts
                without manual intervention.
                For JSON uploads, however, you can specify any category you need directly in the file —
                giving developers full control over structured data.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Reports -->
    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header" id="headingFour">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#collapseFour" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseFour">
                How do I generate reports?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="collapseFour" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingFour"
             data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                Reports can be generated from the Reports page. They can be previewed and downloaded
                as PDFs using integrated PDFSharp.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Data Deletion -->
    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header" id="headingFive">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#collapseFive" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseFive">
                Can I delete my data?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="collapseFive" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingFive"
             data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                Yes. You can delete individual entries from the dashboard or clear all data.
                Deleted entries are permanently removed from the system.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Cost -->
    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header" id="headingSix">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#collapseSix" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseSix">
                Is this app free to use?
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="collapseSix" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingSix"
             data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                Yes. This tool is free to use,with no usage limits, no credit card required, and no upsells and is designed to showcase Blazor, Azure Functions and
                OCR.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header" id="headingSix">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#collapseSeven" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseSeven">
                Who It's For
            </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="collapseSeven" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingSeven"
             data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                ExpenseCategorizer is built for everyday users who deal with receipts that are often
                unorganized or handwritten. These simple, line‑item notes (like "coffee 50" or "gym 600") are
                automatically parsed and categorized without requiring manual setup. Users can see AI‑powered categorization in action, while regular users benefit from quick uploads,
                automatic explanations, and clean reports. Complex business invoices are supported too, but the
                tool shines brightest with handwritten or everyday receipts.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
